    <briefdescription>
<para>Topics related to the µTest++ C++ API. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The µTest++ framework is built upon modern C++ standards, providing a robust and expressive API for defining and managing tests. Its design prioritises clarity and maintainability, offering a concise set of core primitives for verifying expectations and assumptions within test cases.</para>
<para>Unlike many traditional frameworks, µTest++ avoids the use of preprocessor macros; all testing primitives are implemented directly in C++. This approach ensures type safety, improved readability, and seamless integration with contemporary C++ development practices.  </para>
    </detaileddescription>
